& 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1+4)+1(2+4)+3(-4+2) \\\\  & =5+6-6 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -\\frac{19}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}.$" 13194139535585 true] [17592186356181